# ID       : ABOP-025
# Name     : Three-dimensional Hilbert curve
# Source   : chapter 1, book page 20, Fig. 1.19
# Formalism: deterministic bracketed/turtle string
# Parse    : pass
# Execute  : pass
# Note     : 3D turtle commands are ordinary modules to the rewrite engine.
#
# Original ABOP:
# ABOP | ω : A
# ABOP | p1    : A -> B-F+CFC+F-D&F^D-F+&&CFC+F+B//
# ABOP | p2    : B -> A&F^CFB^F^D^^-F-D^|F^B|FC^F^A//
# ABOP | p3    : C -> |D^|F^B-F+C^F^A&&FA&F^C+F+B^F^D//
# ABOP | p4    : D -> |CFB-F+B|FA&F^A&&FB-F+B|FC//
#
axiom A;

match A then B Minus F Plus C F C Plus F Minus D PitchDown F PitchUp D Minus F Plus PitchDown PitchDown C F C Plus F Plus B RollRight RollRight;
match B then A PitchDown F PitchUp C F B PitchUp F PitchUp D PitchUp PitchUp Minus F Minus D PitchUp Around F PitchUp B Around F C PitchUp F PitchUp A RollRight RollRight;
match C then Around D PitchUp Around F PitchUp B Minus F Plus C PitchUp F PitchUp A PitchDown PitchDown F A PitchDown F PitchUp C Plus F Plus B PitchUp F PitchUp D RollRight RollRight;
match D then Around C F B Minus F Plus B Around F A PitchDown F PitchUp A PitchDown PitchDown F B Minus F Plus B Around F C RollRight RollRight;
